Imported memory: honour MAXIMUM_MEMORY without memory growth

Without ALLOW_MEMORY_GROWTH, emcc links with --no-growable-memory, which
declares the memory's maximum equal to its initial size, and lowers a
MAXIMUM_MEMORY the user set to INITIAL_MEMORY with a warning that it means
nothing. For an imported memory it does mean something: the module can run
in a memory of any size from its initial size to its declared maximum, so
one build can take a memory sized when it is loaded, while never growing
it. With IMPORTED_MEMORY and a user-set MAXIMUM_MEMORY, keep the maximum
and pass it to wasm-ld as --max-memory. Everything that depends on growth
(emscripten_resize_heap, getHeapMax, the fallback memory's maximum) stays
as it is without growth, and CAN_ADDRESS_2GB follows the real maximum.

